# Uptime Kuma

## What is Uptime Kuma?

Uptime Kuma is a self-hosted monitoring tool.

I use it in my homelab to check if my websites, services, and devices are online.

For example, Uptime Kuma can monitor:

- Homepage
- Grafana
- Portainer
- Vaultwarden
- Nextcloud
- Traefik
- Other local or public services

If something goes down, Uptime Kuma can show it on the dashboard and can also send notifications if configured.

---

## Why I Installed It

The goal of this project is to make it easier to see the health of my homelab.

Instead of manually checking every website or service, Uptime Kuma gives me one dashboard where I can quickly see what is working and what is down.

This is useful because my homelab has multiple services running behind Traefik and Docker.

---

## How It Works in My Homelab

Uptime Kuma runs as a Docker container on my Raspberry Pi.

It is available in two ways:

### Local Access

```text
http://192.168.50.199:3002
```

Domain Access
https://uptime.anthonylearchive.com

The domain version works through Traefik.

Traefik receives the request for:

uptime.anthonylearchive.com

Then Traefik sends the request to the Uptime Kuma container.

Traefik Labels

The labels tell Traefik how to expose Uptime Kuma through my domain.

- "traefik.enable=true"

This tells Traefik to manage this container.

- "traefik.http.routers.uptime-kuma.rule=Host(`uptime.anthonylearchive.com`)"

This tells Traefik:

When someone visits uptime.anthonylearchive.com, send them to Uptime Kuma.
- "traefik.http.routers.uptime-kuma.entrypoints=websecure"

This tells Traefik to use the HTTPS entrypoint.

- "traefik.http.routers.uptime-kuma.tls=true"

This enables HTTPS.

- "traefik.http.routers.uptime-kuma.tls.certresolver=myresolver"

This tells Traefik to use my working certificate resolver for SSL certificates.

- "traefik.http.services.uptime-kuma.loadbalancer.server.port=3001"

This tells Traefik that Uptime Kuma runs on port 3001 inside the container.

Network
networks:
  - proxy

This connects Uptime Kuma to the same Docker network as Traefik.

At the bottom:

networks:
  proxy:
    external: true

This means the proxy network already exists and is shared with Traefik

Example Services to Monitor

Some services I can add to Uptime Kuma include:

Service	Example URL
Homepage	https://homepage.anthonylearchive.com
Portainer	https://portainer.anthonylearchive.com
Grafana	https://grafana.anthonylearchive.com
Vaultwarden	https://vaultwarden.anthonylearchive.com
Nextcloud	https://nextcloud.anthonylearchive.com
